Package: gspy
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: forensic goroutine-to-syscall inspector for Go processes
 gspy attaches to a running Go process by PID using eBPF uprobes and
 kernel tracepoints, mapping goroutine IDs to active kernel syscalls
 and a captured user-space program counter in real time, resolving
 function names where possible. This is not a complete stack trace.
 .
 The tracer uses kernel uprobes and tracepoints without restarting the
 target process. Instrumentation has overhead. Goroutine IDs are read
 from the Go runtime by BPF probes.
 .
 Features include executable SHA-256 recording in readonly mode,
 JSON output for pipeline integration, and a live terminal UI.
 .
 Requires Linux kernel 5.8 or later with BPF syscall support enabled
 (CONFIG_BPF_SYSCALL=y) and either CAP_BPF + CAP_PERFMON or
 CAP_SYS_ADMIN.
